/** @page tokenizerreleasehistory tokenizer Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section tokenizer_3_0 tokenizer Module Version 3.0

    Initial release, shipped with %Qore 3.0.

    - BPE, WordPiece, and Unigram tokenization models
    - Full HuggingFace \c tokenizer.json support with auto-detection of model type
    - Precompiled normalizer (SentencePiece Darts DoubleArray trie)
    - GPT-2 byte-level BPE with hand-coded pattern matcher
    - Truncation: \c longest_first, \c only_first, \c only_second strategies
    - Padding: \c max_length and batch-longest modes
    - Batch encoding: \c encodeBatch() for multi-text processing
    - Byte-level offset mapping and special tokens mask
    - Added token matching before tokenization pipeline
    - Sentence pair encoding with correct \c token_type_ids
    - O(n log n) BPE merge algorithm using priority queue + doubly linked list
    - Vocabulary access: \c getVocab(), \c getVocabSize(), \c tokenToId(), \c idToToken()
    - Cooperative cancellation support via \c qore_check_cancel()
    - utf8proc-based Unicode normalization (NFC/NFD/NFKC/NFKD) and digit classification
    - Verified against Python \c tokenizers for BERT, GPT-2, T5, and Llama
    - Dense model-input APIs: \c encodeForModel(), \c encodeBatchForModel(),
      and \c encodeBatchPairsForModel() return row-major \c buffer<int64>
      values for direct ONNX tensor creation without per-token list/hash
      materialization
    - \c Replace normalizers support HuggingFace \c {"Regex": "..."} patterns

*/
